    "english":  "The sweet jasmine buds open their white petals in the forest clearings,\nlike the radiant smile of a bashful bride.\nThe black stags skip joyfully with their doe across the green pastures,\ndrunk on the coolness of the fresh seasonal rains.\nThe thunder rolls across the sky, beating like drums of victory,\nheralding the close of the king\u0027s expedition.\nHe promised to return when the golden flowers burst into bloom;\nlook, dear friend, the blossoms are open and the chariot bell rings afarΓÇö\nmy long wait in this lonely cottage is crowned with his return!",
